'''''Arabis''''' {{IPAc-en|ˈ|ær|ə|b|ᵻ|s}},<ref name=":0">''Sunset Western Garden Book,'' 1995:606–607</ref> or '''rockcress''', is a [[genus]] of [[flowering plant]]s, within the family [[Brassicaceae]].

== Description ==
The species are [[herbaceous]], [[annual plant|annual]] or [[perennial plant]]s, growing to {{Convert abbreviated|10-80|cm}} tall, usually densely hairy, with simple entire to lobed [[leaf|leaves]] {{Convert abbreviated|1-6|cm|4=1}} long, and small white four-petaled [[flower]]s. The [[fruit]] is a long, slender [[capsule (fruit)|capsule]] containing 10–20 or more [[seed]]s. Natural habitat for ''Arabis'' species is rocky mountain/cliff sides or dry sites.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web|url=https://pfaf.org/user/Plant.aspx?LatinName=Arabis+caucasica|title=Arabis caucasica Rock Cress, Wall Rockcress PFAF Plant Database|website=pfaf.org|access-date=2019-03-17}}</ref> Cultivation of ''Arabis'' is best suited for rock gardens or container gardens.<ref name=":0" /> This genus is pollinated by members of Apieae and Lepidoptera.<ref name=":1" />
